For my special dinner party, I would invite the following figures from history:

1. Marie Curie - a physicist and chemist who discovered radioactivity and was the first woman to win a Nobel Prize;
2. Martin Luther King Jr. - a Baptist minister and leader of the civil rights movement;
3. Florence Nightingale - the founder of modern nursing and an important figure of the Victorian age;
4. Nelson Mandela - a leader in the anti-apartheid movement and the first black president of South Africa;
5. Frida Kahlo - a Mexican artist known for her self-portraits and vibrant artwork. 

I enjoy all their stories and achievements. Our conversation would be focused on the incredible and challenging things they went through. It would be incredible to talk about hard work and their perseverance and great accomplishments. They are all very inspirational figures.
